><highlight color="#9643FC" opacity="0.399994" creationdate="D:20250709102229+10'00'" flags="print" IT="HighlightNote" date="D:20250709102232+10'00'" name="c3751756-231f-40b0-a227-3d100490b30a" page="3" coords="58.053500,481.957000,290.265000,481.957000,58.053500,471.601000,290.265000,471.601000,58.053500,471.016000,290.279000,471.016000,58.053500,460.660000,290.279000,460.660000,58.053500,460.074000,290.258000,460.074000,58.053500,449.718000,290.258000,449.718000,58.053500,449.132000,290.258000,449.132000,58.053500,438.776000,290.258000,438.776000,58.053500,438.134000,290.168000,438.134000,58.053500,427.778000,290.168000,427.778000,58.053500,427.193000,290.205000,427.193000,58.053500,416.837000,290.205000,416.837000,58.053500,416.251000,290.302000,416.251000,58.053500,405.895000,290.302000,405.895000,58.053500,405.253000,290.277000,405.253000,58.053500,394.897000,290.277000,394.897000,58.053500,394.311000,290.275000,394.311000,58.053500,383.956000,290.275000,383.956000,58.053500,383.370000,290.207000,383.370000,58.053500,373.014000,290.207000,373.014000,58.053500,372.372000,290.205000,372.372000,58.053500,362.016000,290.205000,362.016000,58.053500,361.430000,290.288000,361.430000,58.053500,351.074000,290.288000,351.074000,58.053500,350.489000,290.168000,350.489000,58.053500,340.133000,290.168000,340.133000,58.053500,339.491000,290.255000,339.491000,58.053500,329.135000,290.255000,329.135000,58.053500,328.549000,290.258000,328.549000,58.053500,318.193000,290.258000,318.193000" rect="57.729900,317.869000,290.625000,482.281000" subject="Comment on Text" title="Alexander Gibson"
><contents-richtext
><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2"
><p dir="ltr"
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Q14c: </span
><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-12.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal"
>Although further research is required to elucidate the mechanisms&#xD;supporting the novel findings of this study, the use of&#xD;compression socks with endurance-based exercise may be effective&#xD;at reducing exercise-associated gastrointestinal damage.&#xD;As intestinal damage during exercise has been associated with&#xD;gastrointestinal disturbances, fatigue, inflammation, and reduced&#xD;postprandial amino acids available for muscle repair,&#xD;reducing damage may ultimately benefit recovery and subsequent&#xD;exercise performance. This consideration is vital for&#xD;coaches and athletes, especially when optimal and rapid recovery&#xD;is crucial for performance in subsequent events. Although&#xD;the exact mechanism for this reduction is to be&#xD;elucidated, it seems that strategies to maintain intestinal blood&#xD;flow during exercise, such as compression socks, may be effective&#xD;at reducing exercise-associated gastrointestinal damage.</span
></p
></body
></contents-richtext
><popup flags="print,nozoom,norotate" open="no" page="3" rect="602.986000,389.957000,786.986000,481.957000"
/></highlight
